outputs.exact_statement:
Let $(M,\tau)$ be a type $\mathrm{II}_1$ von Neumann algebra with separable predual and a faithful normal tracial state, and let $\mu$ be the measure supplied by Theorem <a href="#thm:walk" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="thm:walk">3</a>. Suppose that $T:M\to M$ is bounded, linear, and bounded-ball $2$-continuous, and that $$\label{eq:harmonic-map}
 T(x)=\mathbb E_{U\sim\mu}\bigl[T(xU)U^*\bigr]
 \qquad(x\in M).$$ Then $$\label{eq:liouville-conclusion}
 T(x)=T(1)x\qquad(x\in M).$$

Let $(N,\tau)$ be a finite von Neumann algebra with a faithful normal tracial state. Let $R:N\to N$ be bounded and complex linear, and suppose that $$\label{eq:rigidity-continuity}
 \norm{R(x_n)}_2\longrightarrow0
 \quad\text{whenever}\quad
 \sup_n\norm{x_n}<\infty,
 \qquad \norm{x_n}_2\longrightarrow0.$$ Let $(g_j)_{j\geq1}$ be a free Haar family in $N$, and let $a,b\in N$. Suppose that for every nonempty signed word $w=g_{i_1}^{\varepsilon_1}\cdots g_{i_q}^{\varepsilon_q}$ with $\varepsilon_j\in\{1,-1\}$ and pairwise distinct indices $i_1,\ldots,i_q$, $$\label{eq:rigidity-first-letter}
 R(w)=
 \begin{cases}
 aw,&\varepsilon_1=1,\\
 bw,&\varepsilon_1=-1.
 \end{cases}$$ Then $a=b$.

Let $\mathbb F_r$ be the free group on $r$ generators and let $\lambda$ be its left regular representation. For a finitely supported family $(c_w)_{|w|=q}$ on the reduced words of length $q\geq0$, $$\label{eq:rigidity-length}
 \left\|\sum_{|w|=q}c_w\lambda(w)\right\|
 \leq(q+1)\left(\sum_{|w|=q}|c_w|^2\right)^{1/2}.$$ If $g_1,\ldots,g_r$ have free Haar joint moments in a faithfully tracial von Neumann algebra, every scalar-coefficient word polynomial in them has the same norm as the corresponding polynomial in the regular generators. Consequently, <a href="#eq:rigidity-length" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:rigidity-length">[eq:rigidity-length]</a> also holds with $\lambda(w)$ replaced by $w(g)$, and its right-hand side is $(q+1)\norm{\sum_{|w|=q}c_w w(g)}_2$.

The polar part $V$ of $s$ is a unitary in $\widehat N$, and $$\label{eq:rigidity-power-identities}
 S(V^k)=aV^k,\qquad S(V^{-k})=bV^{-k}
 \qquad(k\geq1).$$

For $n\ge2$ and $\psi\in C_b^n(M,zM)$, set $$\label{eq:central-homotopy-formula}
 \begin{split}
 (J_z\psi)(a_1,\ldots,a_{n-1})
 =\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}(-1)^i\psi(&za_1,\ldots,za_{i-1},
 q,qa_i,\\[-2pt]
 &a_{i+1},\ldots,a_{n-1}).
 \end{split}$$ Set $J_z=0$ in degrees zero and one. Then, in every degree, $$\label{eq:central-homotopy-identity}
 dJ_z+J_zd=\operatorname{id}-\operatorname{cut}_z.$$ For $n\ge1$ the degree-$n$ operator satisfies $$\label{eq:central-homotopy-bound}
 \norm{J_z\psi}\le(n-1)\norm{\psi}.$$
